{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#1376","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#1376","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#1376\",\"parent_revision\":\"3477f93b4b67a6617f95cfc968ef2ecad5d6ec32\",\"root_revision\":\"723d19ec3741df6b1735212d29c869034e06f229ff3117aff88cdf87e2e21b57\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nWhen a work-backlog-item session is interrupted (crash, credit exhaustion, power loss, kill), the workflow state is lost. A new session has no record of which phase and step was active, what artifacts existed, or what decisions had been made. The session restarts from the beginning, duplicating work already done (grooming, RT-ICA, discovery, planning).\\n\\nThe problem: no durable checkpoint exists for work-backlog-item workflow progress. Phases 1\u20134 can be expensive to re-execute. There is no way to query what step a session was on, on which machine, or what the state of that step was.\\n\\nVerbatim user report: \\\"tracking work-backlog-item live state and identifying where work is being done and stale states, and where to continue from if interrupted.\\\"\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] When `work-backlog-item {title}` is invoked on an item with `status:in-progress`, the workflow detects the completed phases from durable artifact signals and resumes from the first incomplete phase (not from Step 1)\\n- [ ] Phase completion is inferred from: Phase 2 \u2192 `status:in-progress` + issue# + feature-context artifact; Phase 3 \u2192 groomed date + RT-ICA section with fresh Date:; Phase 4 \u2192 `plan` field pointing to valid SAM plan\\n- [ ] Items interrupted during Phase 5+ (execution) resume via existing Step R (no change needed \u2014 SAM plan captures task progress)\\n- [ ] Resume path is automatic (not a separate command) when the main workflow detects `status:in-progress`\\n- [ ] No duplicate grooming, RT-ICA, or planning for already-completed phases\\n- [ ] `work-backlog-item` SKILL.md documents the resume detection logic\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **work-backlog-item workflow state persistence and resume capability** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session observation \u2014 user request during work-backlog-item session\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-04-01\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-04-04)\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\nP1 \u2014 confirmed. Every interrupted session currently duplicates all prior work. Phase 3 (groom + RT-ICA) is the most expensive re-work; artifact inference makes it skippable.\\n\\n### Scope\\n\\nIn scope:\\n- Phase-inference algorithm at the top of `work-backlog-item` SKILL.md dispatch logic\\n- Skip logic for each phase: if phase N signals are all present \u2192 jump to phase N+1\\n- Documentation of resume detection in SKILL.md\\n\\nOut of scope:\\n- New checkpoint files or directories\\n- Sub-step granularity (step 3.1 vs 3.2 tracking)\\n- Session claim tracking (that is #1369)\\n- Feasibility gate persistence\\n\\n### Files\\n\\nMODIFY:\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/SKILL.md` \u2014 add phase-inference block at workflow entry; document the 4 phase-complete signals; add skip logic before Phase 2, 3, and 4 dispatch\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/step-procedures.md` \u2014 update Step R to cover Phases 1\u20133 (currently Phase 4+ only)\\n\\nNO new files required.\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n- None blocking. #1369 (session-aware work claim) is independent and may be implemented before or after.\\n\\n### Design Decisions\\n\\n1. **Automatic resume** \u2014 the main `work-backlog-item` workflow entry detects `status:in-progress` and runs the phase-inference algorithm before dispatching any agent. No separate `/resume` command.\\n\\n2. **Artifact inference, not explicit checkpoint writes** \u2014 sub-step granularity (e.g., \\\"staleness was COSMETIC_ONLY\\\") is not persisted. The workflow re-derives cheap checks (git log, `backlog_view`) and skips expensive ones (grooming, RT-ICA) when their durable signals are present and fresh.\\n\\n3. **Feasibility gate** \u2014 re-evaluated from groomed sections at resume time (deterministic, low cost). Not persisted separately.\\n\\n4. **Scope boundary with #1369** \u2014 #1369 records who holds the claim (session ID). This item (#1376) records what phase was reached. Independent \u2014 implement in any order. The `active-task-{SESSION_ID}.json` in `context/` is not the checkpoint.\\n\\n### Key Finding: No New Storage Needed\\n\\nThe workflow already leaves durable breadcrumbs at each phase that can be read at resume time:\\n\\n```text\\nPhase 2 complete \u2192 status:in-progress label + issue# present + (feature-context artifact OR type:fix/bug)\\nPhase 3 complete \u2192 groomed date present + RT-ICA section has fresh Date: header + RT-ICA = APPROVED\\nPhase 4 complete \u2192 plan field points to a valid SAM plan file (sam_read succeeds)\\nPhase 5+ complete \u2192 sam_status shows task progress (Step R already handles this)\\n```\\n\\nA reverse-order check (4 \u2192 3 \u2192 2 \u2192 1) at workflow entry identifies the resume point. No new checkpoint files, no new directories, no new schema.\\n\\n### Phase Completion Signals (implementation reference)\\n\\n| Phase | Signal to check | Tool |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Phase 2 | `backlog_view` \u2192 `status` == \\\"in-progress\\\" AND `issue` field present | `backlog_view` |\\n| Phase 3 | `backlog_view.sections[\\\"RT-ICA\\\"]` exists AND contains `Date:` | `backlog_view(summary=false)` |\\n| Phase 4 | `backlog_view` \u2192 `plan` field present AND `sam_read(plan)` succeeds | `backlog_view` + `sam_read` |\\n| Phase 5+ | `sam_status` shows progress | `sam_status` (existing Step R) |\\n\",\"digest\":\"c7b7aa0d87d2e1a5e869ade3fdad2e5509ae678b58c42b4b7ae435bb491ec009\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPnIWWA\"}"}